[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124890,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pigmented epithelioid melanocytomas (PEMs) are melanocytic neoplasms composed of pigmented epithelioid melanocytes, characterized by combined mutational activation of the PKA (protein kinase&nbsp;A) and MAPK (mitogen-activated protein kinase) pathways.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124891,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8780/1 Pigmented epithelioid melanocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124892,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F20.1 &amp; XH4VD0 Atypical melanocytic naevus &amp; Pigmented epithelioid melanocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124893,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> epithelioid blue naevus; <em>PRKAR1A</em>-inactivated melanocytoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> animal-type melanoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124894,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124895,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PEMs arise on the extremities, head and neck, trunk, and (rarely) mucosal sites {23143456}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124896,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PEMs appear as slowly growing pigmented nodules or papules {14707861}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124897,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PEMs are rare tumours. They can occur at any age, most commonly arising in the second and third decades of life {14707861}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124898,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PEMs can occur sporadically or in patients with Carney complex {8772778}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124899,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately two&nbsp;thirds of PEMs have inactivating genetic alterations in <em>PRKAR1A</em> {18059235; 28796000; 30475255; 35319526} in addition to one of several activating mutations of the MAPK pathway {30475255; 35319526}. <em>PRKAR1A</em> inactivation constitutively activates PKA and induces melanocyte proliferation, differentiation, and pigmentation {32118628; 32682887}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124900,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124901,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "<p>Most PEMs are heavily pigmented, predominantly dermal tumours, with an inverted wedge or bulbous configuration. Small junctional nests are seen in 30% of cases, often with accompanying epidermal hyperplasia. They are composed of pigmented dendritic and epithelioid melanocytes with vesicular nuclei that have prominent nucleoli, sometimes resembling Reed&ndash;Sternberg cells or fried eggs. The epithelioid cells can show substantial nuclear polymorphism and multinucleation and may have diminished pigmentation.</p>\r\n<p>The term &ldquo;atypical PEM&rdquo; may be applied to lesions with severe histological atypia and/or genomic aberrations suggestive of progression towards melanoma.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Loss of expression of PRKAR1A is found in as many as 80% of cases {18059235}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes blue naevus with epithelioid cells {22892599}, blue naevus with <em>PRKCA</em> fusion, melanoma (metastatic or primary), Spitz naevus, and WNT-activated melanocytoma. Tumours with fusions of <em>PRKCA</em> or with other mutations in the G<sub>q</sub>&alpha; pathway can have histological phenotypes resembling PEMs. As mutational activation of the G<sub>q</sub>&alpha; pathway is pathognomonic of blue naevi, neoplasms with <em>PRKCA</em> fusions {26676968; 28796000; 30475255; 31437301} are not classified as PEMs but are instead classified with blue naevi and related neoplasms, unless they also have mutations in the PKA pathway {35319526}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:42:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124902,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124903,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DNA- and RNA-based sequencing helps to establish the diagnosis of PEM by confirming the presence of <em>PRKAR1A</em> inactivating mutations and rule out the presence of molecular markers of progression towards melanoma such as <em>TERT</em> promoter mutations or <em>CDKN2A</em> inactivation in atypical presentations.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124904,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a proliferation of pigmented dendritic and epithelioid melanocytes admixed with melanophages.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> demonstration of <em>PRKAR1A</em> inactivation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124905,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124906,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 52,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PEMs are melanocytic tumours of low to intermediate malignant potential {19773637}. Spread to regional sentinel lymph nodes was found in 46% of cases, more commonly in cases with ulceration {14707861; 19773637}. Distant metastases are extremely rare. The prognosis is excellent, even in cases with lymph node metastases {19773637}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T16:41:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]